Q1. Identify the statement(s) in which *CONTENTIOUS* has been used correctly.

I. The contentious nature of the bilateral trade agreement necessitated protracted negotiations spanning multiple fiscal quarters.

II. The scholar's contentious thesis, though methodologically sound, provoked vehement opposition from established academic circles.

III. Despite contentious beginnings, the merger proceeded smoothly with unanimous stakeholder approval.

👉🏻 Select correct option
Only I and II ✅
Only II and III
Only I and III
All I, II and III
Ex: Contentious means causing disagreement. Statement III contradicts itself by suggesting smooth proceedings after contentious beginnings without resolution.

